From: SC130 platform integration
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drm: zynqmp: restore vblank only for active modesets

atomic_begin runs for every plane commit. Calling drm_crtc_vblank_on()
unconditionally resets the software timestamp and adds a synthetic count
before the actual vblank IRQ, making each framebuffer flip advance the
sequence twice.

Keep restoration in atomic_begin because this driver's default commit tail
runs plane begin/flush before modeset enables; moving it to atomic_enable
would leave the initial atomic_flush event without an enabled vblank.
Restore only when the new CRTC is active and needs a modeset, matching the
atomic helper's enable filtering. atomic_disable already calls vblank_off.

Regression cases: active framebuffer-only updates do not restore; initial
activation/resume, active mode changes and connector changes restore once;
inactive/disable updates leave vblank off. Physical frame timing is unchanged.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/zynqmp_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/zynqmp_kms.c
@@ -338,6 +338,13 @@ static void zynqmp_dpsub_crtc_atomic_begin(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 					   struct drm_atomic_state *state)
 {
-	drm_crtc_vblank_on(crtc);
+	/*
+	 * Plane-only updates must not reset the software vblank count.
+	 * Restore before atomic_flush arms the event, but only when an active
+	 * modeset enables the CRTC after atomic_disable turned vblank off.
+	 */
+	if (crtc->state->active &&
+	    drm_atomic_crtc_needs_modeset(crtc->state))
+		drm_crtc_vblank_on(crtc);
 }
 
 static void zynqmp_dpsub_crtc_atomic_flush(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
